rules:
  - id: webrtc-ice-servers-camelcase
    class: inject
    when: { write: "*.yaml", contains-any: ["webrtc_config", "webRtcConfig", "ice_servers", "iceServers"] }
    dedupe-of: "scripts/ci/validate-conductor-config.sh (the deterministic render/deploy gate that rejects the dead key by name)"
    why: >
      INVARIANT — `webrtc_config` passes VERBATIM into tx5's serde-camelCase `WebRtcConfig`.
      The ICE-server list key MUST be `iceServers` (camelCase). The snake_case `ice_servers`
      is an UNKNOWN field: serde silently drops it and the conductor runs with ZERO ICE servers
      — WebRTC survives on host candidates only while peers are co-located, then dies silently
      when topology spreads (adam→shem, 2026-05-27; 2,081 divergent anchors from the co-located
      era). Use `iceServers`, never `ice_servers`. The render gate
      `scripts/ci/validate-conductor-config.sh` enforces this at deploy; do not ship a manifest
      it will reject. Evidence: Holochain conductor-config example (`iceServers`); tx5-connection
      `config.rs` `#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]`.
  - id: resource-limit-raise-design-signal
    class: ask
    when: { write: "*.yaml" }
    validator: epr:validator-resource-limit-raise-design-signal
    retire-when: >
      when demand has a native home and the gate can READ it instead of projecting it — an
      `Envelope::demand` beside `Envelope::bound` in ark-core, rendered by bridges/k8s the way the
      bound is rendered today — so a raise past the modelled demand fails at render rather than at
      review. Only the recurrence count would remain, and `resource-limit-raises@1` carries that.
    why: >
      Raising a CPU or memory LIMIT is System 1 amplifying the regulator. Ashby admits that move
      — a regulator needs the variety of what it regulates, and either attenuating the disturbance
      or amplifying the regulator restores the balance — so this rule never says a raise is wrong.
      What it does not admit is amplifying again and again while the disturbance at the source is
      never attenuated: Meadows' shifting-the-burden-to-the-intervenor. The raise is therefore
      treated as ALGEDONIC evidence (elohim/epr/src/algedonic.rs) — APPROACH at the band edge,
      BREACH past it — and REFERRED to the design plane (S3/S4) rather than answered on the
      operational one. It carries a NUMBER, not a questionnaire: requested vs a demand model
      composed from the deviceArchetype canonical budget, a ratified `resourceOverride` read from
      the PRE-state, the Rakia `limits.cpu_m` overcommit ratification, the `bridges/k8s::share()`
      split, the declared `edgenodeArcFactor` and the declared hosted cast — plus the count of
      prior raise stamps this unit already carries. Never fires on a lower or equal value, a new
      unit, an unparseable edit, or a YAML no deployment record claims.
cites:
  - substrate-convergence-five-defect-arc
